  "solution": {
    "text": "For a short bar magnet in tan A&nbsp;position,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>tan&#952;</mi><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math>...(i)<br /><br />When distance is doubled, then new deflection <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8242;</mi></math> is given by,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>tan&#952;</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></math> ....(ii)<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan&#160;</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msup> <mi>&#952;</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan&#160;</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"norm